   {
    "quote": "Selective reporting of pre-specified outcomes – depending on the nature and direction of the analysed results – occurs among a large proportion of published clinical trials, resulting in outcome reporting bias. Selective reporting of outcomes can potentially compromise the validity of a trial and any subsequent meta-analyses.",
